cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Skill Trees
message: >-
  If you use this software or the material in it, please cite the tagged
  release you used rather than the main branch.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vidar
    family-names: Skogvoll
    email: vidarsko@uio.no
    affiliation: University of Oslo
repository-code: https://github.com/vidarsko/ai-skill-trees
url: https://aiskilltrees.com
abstract: >-
  A skill tree is a graph of the skills and concepts in one school subject,
  written by a teacher, with an instruction on each node that a student copies
  into an AI chat. This repository holds the rendering engine, the
  instructions, the interface languages and the decomposition model.
keywords:
  - education
  - open educational resources
  - prompt engineering
  - prerequisite graph
